From 27868e48973766c76b4711ea1d75175ce718468f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bob <robertramsay78@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:23:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Pro: Animate page - Idle, Walk, Jump and Fall animations of
 up to 8 frames

Engine data version 5: actor record 52 bytes with A_ANIM, an animation table
per actor (4 x 72 bytes: frames, rate, loop / once / ping-pong, frame offsets
facing right and left). place_sprites picks the animation from what the actor
is doing (Jump / Fall in the air for platform players, hoppers and fallers)
and turns the frames round while it moves left. Per-actor engine state grows
to 64 bytes (v_fofs, v_aset, v_astart, v_face).

The two-frame animation of older projects is written as a table too, so old
games play as before (checked in FS-UAE with the five examples); a hopper's
crouch frame stays A_SPR2. The Animate page (Lite sees it with a Pro note)
picks frames from the sprite bank with a live 50 Hz preview.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BQFSzGarhTTpK2DHf8XzFr
